<title>JAPAN: Yaohan shares climb on bargain-hunting.</title>
<headline>Yaohan shares climb on bargain-hunting.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Yaohan Japan Corp jumped on Thursday morning, helped by bargain-hunting after its recent sharp slides, traders said.</p>
<p>The share price of the supermarket chain operator was up 19 yen at 435 yen at 0046 GMT. Volume was 2.12 million shares.</p>
<p>Japan Securities Finance Co Ltd said on Wednesday that it had issued a &quot;warning&quot; that it may run short of shares in Yaohan Japan Corp to lend for margin trade, but that has had little impact on the shares so far, the traders said.</p>
</text>
